      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Illinois Central Railroad ran through Hackleburg in the early 1900s, sparking a train station and worker housing that lasted until the station closed in 1968.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/hackleburg/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hackleburg marks the highest point—931 feet above sea level—along the historic route connecting Miami, Florida, with Chicago, Illinois.",
